.TH PORTBRIDGE 1 "2026" "portbridge 1.0.0" "PortBridge Manual"
.SH NAME
portbridge \- manage TCP port forwarding to the public internet via Tailscale Funnel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portbridge
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B portbridge
exposes a TCP service listening on this Linux machine to ordinary internet
TCP clients, without requiring the remote machine to install any VPN
client or special software. It does this by driving the official
.B tailscale
CLI's Funnel feature: this machine joins your private Tailscale network
(tailnet) and Tailscale's infrastructure publishes one of your local ports
to a fixed, small set of public TCP ports on your tailnet's
.I *.ts.net
hostname. Only this machine ever needs Tailscale installed; a remote user
connects with a plain TCP client such as
.BR nc (1).
.PP
portbridge never inspects, modifies, or executes anything received over
the forwarded connection \(em it forwards raw TCP bytes only.
.PP
Because Tailscale Funnel is restricted by the provider to external TCP
ports 443, 8443, and 10000, portbridge will refuse to silently substitute
a different port when you request one that isn't supported; instead it
explains the restriction and asks you to choose an allowed port.
.PP
With no command, portbridge launches an interactive menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Check whether Tailscale is installed, its background service is running,
and this device is authenticated -- offering to fix each gap
interactively (installing Tailscale, starting
.BR tailscaled ,
running
.BR "tailscale up" )
with a confirmation prompt before each action. Never proceeds on its own
in a non-interactive context unless
.B \-\-yes
is given.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes on all confirmation prompts.
.RE
.TP
.B start
Start TCP port forwarding. Prompts interactively for anything not given on
the command line.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-\-port =\fIPORT\fR
Local port to forward.
.TP
.BR \-\-external\-port =\fIPORT\fR
Requested public port (must be 443, 8443, or 10000).
.TP
.BR \-\-bind =\fIADDRESS\fR
Local bind address (default 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.BR \-\-mode =\fIMODE\fR
.I tcp
(raw TCP forwarder, default) or
.I tls\-terminated\-tcp
(Tailscale terminates TLS at the edge).
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Run in the foreground instead of detaching a background monitor. Intended
for use as a systemd
.B ExecStart
command.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes on all confirmation prompts (for scripting).
.RE
.TP
.B stop
Stop TCP port forwarding started by portbridge. Never affects the local
service listening on the forwarded port, and never affects processes
portbridge did not start.
.TP
.B status
Print a detailed status report: Tailscale install/auth/connection state,
whether the local port is listening, current forwarding status, the
public endpoint, uptime, and a health checklist.
.TP
.B endpoint
Print the current public endpoint as
.IR host:port .
.TP
.B test
Test connectivity.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-local
Test only the local port.
.TP
.B \-\-external
Test only the external (public) endpoint.
.TP
.BR \-\-port =\fIPORT\fR
Override which local port to test.
.RE
.TP
.B logs
Show recent log entries from
.IR ~/.local/state/portbridge/portbridge.log .
.RS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-follow
Follow the log live (like
.BR "tail \-f" ).
.TP
.BR \-n =\fIN\fR
Number of lines to show (default 50).
.RE
.TP
.B restart
Stop (if running) and start again using the previously stored
configuration.
.TP
.B configure
Interactive configuration wizard, or pass flags (see
.BR "portbridge configure \-\-help" )
to set specific values non\-interactively.
.TP
.B listen
Run a disposable TCP echo listener for testing, completely separate from
forwarding management. Equivalent in spirit to
.BR "nc \-l \-p PORT" .
Requires
.BR \-\-port .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/portbridge/config.toml
User configuration (bind address, default ports, health\-check/backoff
timings, logging level). Contains no secrets.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/portbridge/state.json
Current runtime state: whether forwarding is active, the monitor PID,
configured ports, public hostname, start time, and health.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/portbridge/portbridge.log
Rotating log file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
on a handled error (message printed to stderr),
.B 130
if interrupted with Ctrl+C.
.SH SECURITY
portbridge never stores Tailscale authentication tokens; login is
delegated entirely to
.B tailscale up
/
.BR "tailscale login" .
It never scans the network, never opens ports you did not request, never
modifies local firewall rules, and never executes anything received over
the forwarded TCP connection.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tailscale (1),
.BR nc (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.br
Tailscale Funnel documentation: https://tailscale.com/kb/1223/funnel
